                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>本课程以理论课授课为主，开设部分讨论课和实验课，加深对理论知识的理解。</p>
<p>一、<strong>理论课（50学时）</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;授课的内容分为四大方面的内容，包括神经细胞生物学，神经递质与受体，神经生理功能和神经系统重大疾病的生物学基础。</p>
<p><strong>医学神经科学概述 </strong>（2学时）</p>
<p><strong>神经细胞生物学</strong>重点讲授（共4学时）：神经细胞的结构及血脑屏障，神经元的电活动原理，神经细胞信息传递原理及其新技术发展(2)；神经系统发育(2)。</p>
<p><strong>神经递质与受体</strong>重点讲解（共14学时）：神经递质氨基酸递质（2）；单胺类递质（4）；胆碱能递质，神经系统对内脏活动的调节（2）；神经肽（4）；其他递质（2）。</p>
<p><strong>神经生理功能</strong>重点介绍（共18学时）：痛觉及镇痛药（2）；特殊感觉功能及其调节机制（2）；神经系统对运动的调节（4）；植物神经功能调节药物（2）；脑电活动，睡眠与觉醒的神经机制，癫痫（2）；镇静催眠和抗癫痫药（2））；学习和记忆（4）。</p>
<p><strong>神经系统疾病生物学基础</strong>重点介绍（共12学时）： 脑疾病的病理学总论（4）；神经免疫（2）；脑卒中的损伤和修复（2）；老年认知障碍（2）；帕金森病（2）。</p>
<p><strong>二、实验课：</strong>共开设3个实验（12学时实验课），要求结合理论课的授课时间，安排相应的实验课，深化对理论知识的掌握。</p>
<p>1.神经纤维束动作电位电生理实验，大脑皮层诱发电位和脑电活动（4）；</p>
<p>2.组织学实验（皮肤眼耳）（4）；</p>
<p>3.神经疾病的病理学总论（4）</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:70.8500pt;">
                <td width=205 valign=center colspan=4 style="width:123.1000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-left-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋">课程简介（英文）</font></span></b><b
                                style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                    <p class=MsoNormal align=center style="text-align:center;"><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">Course </font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">Description</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-spacerun:'yes';">&nbsp;</span></span></b><b><span
                                    style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">(</span></b><b><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-ascii-font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-hansi-font-family:'Times New Roman';
mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-weight:bold;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="Times New Roman">in English</font></span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;">)</span></b><b><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>

                </td>
                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">This course primarily consists of theoretical lectures, supplemented by discussion sessions and laboratory classes to deepen understanding of theoretical knowledge.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">I. Theoretical Lectures (50 h)</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">The curriculum covers four major areas: neuronal cell biology, neurotransmitters and receptors, neurophysiological functions, and the biological basis of major neurological disorders.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Overview of Medical Neuroscience (2 h)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Key Topics in Neuronal Cell Biology (4 h):</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Structure of Neuronal Cells and the Blood-Brain Barrier</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Principles of Neuronal Electrical Activity</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Mechanisms of Neuronal Signal Transmission and Emerging Technologies (2 h)</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Development of the Nervous System (2 h)</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Key Topics in Neurotransmitters and Receptors (14 h):</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">- Amino Acid Neurotransmitters (2 h) monoamine neurotransmitters (4); cholinergic neurotransmitters and nervous system regulation of visceral functions (2); neuropeptides (4); other neurotransmitters (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Key Topics in Neurophysiological Functions (18 h):</span><br><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Pain perception and analgesics (2); special sensory functions and their regulatory mechanisms (2); nervous system regulation of movement (4); drugs regulating autonomic nervous system functions (2) ; EEG activity, neural mechanisms of sleep and wakefulness, epilepsy (2); Sedatives, hypnotics, and antiepileptic drugs (2); Learning and memory (4).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">Key Topics in Biological Basis of Neurological Disorders (12 h): General pathology of brain diseases (4); Neuroimmunology (2); Injury and repair in stroke (2); Geriatric cognitive impairment (2); Parkinson's disease (2).</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">II. Laboratory Sessions: Three experiments (12 h) shall be conducted, scheduled in conjunction with theoretical lectures to deepen understanding of theoretical knowledge.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">1. Electrophysiological experiments on nerve fiber bundle action potentials, cortical evoked potentials, and EEG activity (4);</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">2. Histology experiments (skin, eye, ear) (4);</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;">3. General pathology of neurological diseases (4).</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:19.9000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
